# Mutation statements accept nested targets like `item N of L`.
constant grid is list of (list of 1, 2, 3), (list of 4, 5, 6)
change item 2 of item 1 of grid to 20
append 7 to item 2 of grid
prepend 0 to item 1 of grid
insert 99 at 2 in item 2 of grid
remove item 1 from item 2 of grid
say grid
# The row is a reference: an alias sees the changes.
constant row is item 1 of grid
append 100 to item 1 of grid
say row
